Package: randolist
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible, Blinded Block Randomisation Lists for Clinical Trials
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hung", "Tran", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "thaihung.tran306@gmail.com"),
    person("Marcel", "Wolbers", role = "aut",
           comment = "original createRandoList()"),
    person("Khanh", "Trinh Dong Huu", role = "aut",
           comment = "patient ID permutation and composite strata"),
    person("OUCRU Biostatistics Group", role = "ctb"))
Description: Creates (stratified) permuted block randomisation lists with
    random block lengths, following the OUCRU SOP PR-BST-DM-001 on creating
    randomisation lists. This is a revision of the legacy
    'createRandoListNew.R' utility that produces identical lists for the
    same seed and settings, fixes a bug that could duplicate patient IDs
    when IDs are permuted, restores the caller's random number generator
    settings, validates inputs, and adds helpers that enforce the SOP's
    dummy/final separation, file naming and verification steps.
